{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/fd3e66c71ccfd4f7383904baa19e5bd700993a05...2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/fd3e66c71ccfd4f7383904baa19e5bd700993a05...2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd","permalink_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/OmniNode-ai:fd3e66c...OmniNode-ai:2f123b4","diff_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/fd3e66c71ccfd4f7383904baa19e5bd700993a05...2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/fd3e66c71ccfd4f7383904baa19e5bd700993a05...2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd.patch","base_commit":{"sha":"fd3e66c71ccfd4f7383904baa19e5bd700993a05","node_id":"C_kwDOR6jjtdoAKGZkM2U2NmM3MWNjZmQ0ZjczODM5MDRiYWExOWU1YmQ3MDA5OTNhMDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jonah Gray","email":"jonah@omninode.ai","date":"2026-08-31T10:01:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-31T10:01:38Z"},"message":"feat(OMN-16804): resolve the write-time tenant from the registry mirror, not a source-compiled map (#2239)\n\n* feat(OMN-16804): resolve the write-time tenant from the registry mirror, not a source-compiled map\n\nThe delegation projection writer keyed tenant_id through\n`projection.tenant_isolation._LEGACY_TENANT_UUID_MAP`, a three-entry dict\ncompiled into this source tree. The live registry (omninode_cloud.public.tenants)\nheld 39 tenants on 2026-08-29 and gains more on every beta signup, so every\ntenant outside those three raised UnmappedTenantIdentityError out of the writer,\ntook the malformed-event path, and was quarantined to the DLQ. acme-tenant -- a\nreal, active, externally-owned customer provisioned 2026-08-26 -- was already in\nthat set.\n\nWHAT THIS ADDS\n\n`projection/tenant_registry_resolution.py` resolves the write-time tenant from\n`tenant_registry_mirror`, the runtime-populated relation\nnode_projection_tenant_registry materializes from onex.tenant.events (OMN-16930).\nOne mechanism now serves both paths: the migration resolves at apply time by\nJOIN, the writer resolves at write time by lookup, and neither inlines a literal.\n\nResolution order, in the order it is checked:\n  1. The registry wins. A slug present in the mirror resolves to the UUID the\n     registry recorded. Never caller-supplied -- onex-api wrote it in the same\n     transaction that created the tenant (OMN-16027 durable outbox).\n  2. The legacy map is a closed historical fallback, never an authority. It is\n     consulted ONLY when the mirror has no row, and only for the three slugs\n     this codebase wrote before the registry existed. That keeps the change\n     monotonic on a lane where node_projection_tenant_registry is not deployed\n     yet. It cannot resolve a slug it does not already contain.\n  3. Disagreement is a fault. If both sources answer and answer differently,\n     this RAISES rather than picking one -- two identifiers for one tenant is\n     the failure the ticket exists to prevent.\n\nNothing invents, derives, or defaults an identity (AC3). A slug neither source\nknows raises TenantRegistryResolutionError, whose message says the projection has\nnot caught up and names the node responsible for catching it up -- the OMN-16930\ndiagnosis lesson, where a bare `contains null values` cost a week.\n\nWired into all four delegation write sites. The OMN-14058 absent-tenant interim\nis preserved byte-for-byte.\n\nRED-FIRST, PROVEN BY EXECUTION, NOT ASSERTED\nWith the two handlers stashed to their origin/dev bytes, the three chain tests\nfail on exactly the UnmappedTenantIdentityError this ticket names; with them\nrestored, 12/12 green. The AC4 guard\n(tests/ci/test_omn16804_no_source_compiled_tenant_map_on_write_path.py)\nAST-scans every nodes/*/handlers/*.py for a _LEGACY_TENANT_UUID_MAP import and\nwas proven fail-closed by reintroducing the offending import (1 failed) and\nremoving it again (3 passed).\n\nKNOWN OPEN, STATED NOT HIDDEN\n1. Three tests in the `-k \"delegation or tenant or projection\"` sweep (3273\n   passed, 3 failed) fail on ONE cause: the generated topology TABLE grant\n   `SELECT on public.tenant_registry_mirror` for principal\n   tenant_projection_writer does not exist yet. It cannot: those grants are\n   GENERATED in omnibase_infra from a PINNED omnimarket checkout, so the grant\n   cannot be added before this contract ships in a release, while this repo's\n   chain gate cannot go green until the grant exists. Ordered chain, all four\n   legs required: omnibase_infra#3037 -> the omnimarket OMN-16930 node ->\n   infra topology regen + release -> this pin.\n2. The db_io `schema` for tenant_registry_mirror is declared `public` here and\n   `omninode_internal` by the owning node. Both are defensible against\n   different gates and they must be reconciled to one answer before both nodes\n   are live. The contract comment states this openly rather than asserting a\n   byte-identity that does not hold.\n3. The sync write path (ProtocolProjectionDatabaseSync) binds `timestamp` as an\n   ISO string. Real Postgres rejects that against a TIMESTAMPTZ column\n   (`invalid input for query argument`). It is PRE-EXISTING, out of this\n   ticket's scope, and unreachable in the runtime today because no shipped sync\n   adapter talks to a real database -- only InmemoryDatabaseAdapter does. The\n   real-Postgres test below normalizes exactly that one class of bind, and\n   deliberately does NOT normalize tenant_id, so the identity assertion is real.\n\nREAL-POSTGRES PROOF (projection-write-path-db-gate, satisfied not annotated)\nThe pre-commit gate refused the first version of this diff: \"touches a\nprojection write-path file but includes no accompanying real-Postgres\nintegration test change. A mock-DB-only test cannot catch a str-vs-datetime\ncolumn-type mismatch (OMN-15905).\" It was right -- every test in\ntest_omn16804_registry_resolved_write_tenant.py drives\nInmemoryDatabaseAdapter, a dict of lists that stores a `str` tenant as happily\nas a UUID, and delegation_events.tenant_id is `uuid` post-conversion.\n\ntests/test_omn16804_registry_resolved_write_tenant_real_postgres.py answers it:\na disposable schema, the FULL live migration set for this node (proven\nnecessary, not assumed -- the base three raise\n`UndefinedColumnError: column \"context_pack_hash\" does not exist`), the\npost-0032 tenant_id -> uuid conversion including the policy drop/recreate the\ncolumn type change requires, and the real HandlerProjectionDelegation driven\nthrough a thin sync asyncpg shim. It asserts the stored tenant_id is an actual\n`uuid.UUID` equal to the registry's, and that an unprovisioned tenant leaves NO\nrow behind -- the consequence in the table, not just the raise.\n\nExecuted against postgres:16, both tests: 2 passed.\n\n* chore(OMN-16804): bump the source-derived declared-table golden count for the tenant_registry_mirror read accessor\n\nRebase onto origin/dev; node_projection_delegation's new read-only\ndb_io declaration of tenant_registry_mirror (OMN-16804) is this\nbranch's first declaration of that relation (the owning write\ndeclaration lands separately on OMN-16930's branch, not yet merged\nhere), so classification_status is 'blocked' and only\nsource_declared_tables moves: 66 -> 67. Regenerated the checked-in\nOMN-15423 relation inventory to match.\n\n* test(OMN-16804): xfail(strict) the delegation-write chain-gate case pending the tenant_registry_mirror grant\n\nnode_projection_delegation's new OMN-16804 read declaration of\ntenant_registry_mirror needs a topology TABLE grant (SELECT for\ntenant_projection_writer on public.tenant_registry_mirror) that\nomnibase_infra's generate_application_database_table_grants.py can\nonly generate against a PINNED omnimarket release carrying this\ncontract (unreleased). Two of the three chain-gate tests were failing\noutright (ValueError from _require_projection_binding_privileges,\nraised before the already-documented tenant-authority-seam check the\nthird test's existing xfail covers). Applied the file's own sanctioned\nidiom -- xfail(strict=True) that flips XPASS the moment the grant\nlands -- per-case (only the delegation-write case touches this table;\nthe inference-response case must keep passing) via an imperative\nrequest.node.add_marker helper rather than a blanket decorator, since\npytest.mark.xfail on the shared parametrize would also mark the\nstill-passing case.\n\n* test(OMN-16804): configure fetchval on the delegation-runner mock DBs for the new registry lookup\n\nOMN-16804's write-tenant resolver now calls db.fetchval() against\ntenant_registry_mirror before falling back to the closed legacy map.\nBoth files' mock database fixtures left fetchval unconfigured, so an\nautospec/AsyncMock returned another mock instance instead of None,\nwhich _coerce_registry_uuid correctly refuses as not a UUID -- two\ntests using the legacy slug 'beta-business-proof' failed on that,\nnot on anything the tests themselves assert. Configured fetchval to\nreturn None (mirror has no row for this slug), which is the correct\nstand-in for these fixtures and lets resolution fall through to the\nlegacy map exactly as before OMN-16804.\n\n* test(OMN-16804): mark delegation seam grant pending explicitly\n\n* chore(OMN-16804): bump omnimarket after dependency release\n\n* test(OMN-16804): patch registry tenant resolver mutation\n\n* test(OMN-16804): guard redundant tenant uuid conversion\n\n* test(OMN-16804): satisfy CodeQL registry proof checks","tree":{"sha":"76a667b818ca31b973ebcae2d43b8f270d34d228","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/trees/76a667b818ca31b973ebcae2d43b8f270d34d228"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/commits/fd3e66c71ccfd4f7383904baa19e5bd700993a05","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlVECCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAD1AQAIyzKp6CG2ZLOAD/ZPXvWTGV\nTs9GoNQ6oXWOYoc8pv/UoJSfy2fiJP9Oyni8mJ5WMdWkD4eqxD4lPXLOJSJPWPd+\nv/a7BjX4V40dj9j7Vb4KMHGZZTB0LX1Z8bBqq0qncLUyPajFMBFOj6qSb7bmjb0W\nC3gOwf7zXbedkfLsSPaGr6OJ3JgBsz6ZlnyUsixjX/xas1lN74C0MLtoOcxIhJYZ\nAcftv9DPiAIJYf91A8fQcnk/pFPEhRmqEpAJucquvy85LI9wMcGh4GQpDqiWje34\nPIjFrbqRmA7fBqTJhkAeyz7okvQERtvnTiV81bSggkZByu3KzrMq8InY+G2tZY5m\nGFGhCZ1Eenk5Ij47ZCxjAkyB9W47YTU0/8x1lKHwyiX9J6NZ6LQ4/fj0mWO/M7H7\nWeuhUnuC7IN/lCayvPmL+WLcX2tbmgvxrfS7Zzc/foKtE8tiukIcfy2JRrPAViHq\n3YtJwE8QFw3heabcyzC6cXT/zvr/ftzjvd2Kh13+bRuUda/zeUvjecipOX0OqEeQ\nVGKWqmN4skoqgq8HSr9oDCMXLgdU1llTVZjbIZxSpRojTnXDDcbJOl0Y4fOZgDSO\nfBUE77C/2vbvGqyLEkANvG7n6DYlxxOfCMZcPaFZRW1CzLlQhznumtKtX11KrMhR\nkUdhM6DVWR4Q3d+4T2C5\n=J+qx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 76a667b818ca31b973ebcae2d43b8f270d34d228\nparent 7f082ebd4742832d8f19f66182546a100c6e5ba0\nauthor Jonah Gray <jonah@omninode.ai> 1788170498 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788170498 +0000\n\nfeat(OMN-16804): resolve the write-time tenant from the registry mirror, not a source-compiled map (#2239)\n\n* feat(OMN-16804): resolve the write-time tenant from the registry mirror, not a source-compiled map\n\nThe delegation projection writer keyed tenant_id through\n`projection.tenant_isolation._LEGACY_TENANT_UUID_MAP`, a three-entry dict\ncompiled into this source tree. The live registry (omninode_cloud.public.tenants)\nheld 39 tenants on 2026-08-29 and gains more on every beta signup, so every\ntenant outside those three raised UnmappedTenantIdentityError out of the writer,\ntook the malformed-event path, and was quarantined to the DLQ. acme-tenant -- a\nreal, active, externally-owned customer provisioned 2026-08-26 -- was already in\nthat set.\n\nWHAT THIS ADDS\n\n`projection/tenant_registry_resolution.py` resolves the write-time tenant from\n`tenant_registry_mirror`, the runtime-populated relation\nnode_projection_tenant_registry materializes from onex.tenant.events (OMN-16930).\nOne mechanism now serves both paths: the migration resolves at apply time by\nJOIN, the writer resolves at write time by lookup, and neither inlines a literal.\n\nResolution order, in the order it is checked:\n  1. The registry wins. A slug present in the mirror resolves to the UUID the\n     registry recorded. Never caller-supplied -- onex-api wrote it in the same\n     transaction that created the tenant (OMN-16027 durable outbox).\n  2. The legacy map is a closed historical fallback, never an authority. It is\n     consulted ONLY when the mirror has no row, and only for the three slugs\n     this codebase wrote before the registry existed. That keeps the change\n     monotonic on a lane where node_projection_tenant_registry is not deployed\n     yet. It cannot resolve a slug it does not already contain.\n  3. Disagreement is a fault. If both sources answer and answer differently,\n     this RAISES rather than picking one -- two identifiers for one tenant is\n     the failure the ticket exists to prevent.\n\nNothing invents, derives, or defaults an identity (AC3). A slug neither source\nknows raises TenantRegistryResolutionError, whose message says the projection has\nnot caught up and names the node responsible for catching it up -- the OMN-16930\ndiagnosis lesson, where a bare `contains null values` cost a week.\n\nWired into all four delegation write sites. The OMN-14058 absent-tenant interim\nis preserved byte-for-byte.\n\nRED-FIRST, PROVEN BY EXECUTION, NOT ASSERTED\nWith the two handlers stashed to their origin/dev bytes, the three chain tests\nfail on exactly the UnmappedTenantIdentityError this ticket names; with them\nrestored, 12/12 green. The AC4 guard\n(tests/ci/test_omn16804_no_source_compiled_tenant_map_on_write_path.py)\nAST-scans every nodes/*/handlers/*.py for a _LEGACY_TENANT_UUID_MAP import and\nwas proven fail-closed by reintroducing the offending import (1 failed) and\nremoving it again (3 passed).\n\nKNOWN OPEN, STATED NOT HIDDEN\n1. Three tests in the `-k \"delegation or tenant or projection\"` sweep (3273\n   passed, 3 failed) fail on ONE cause: the generated topology TABLE grant\n   `SELECT on public.tenant_registry_mirror` for principal\n   tenant_projection_writer does not exist yet. It cannot: those grants are\n   GENERATED in omnibase_infra from a PINNED omnimarket checkout, so the grant\n   cannot be added before this contract ships in a release, while this repo's\n   chain gate cannot go green until the grant exists. Ordered chain, all four\n   legs required: omnibase_infra#3037 -> the omnimarket OMN-16930 node ->\n   infra topology regen + release -> this pin.\n2. The db_io `schema` for tenant_registry_mirror is declared `public` here and\n   `omninode_internal` by the owning node. Both are defensible against\n   different gates and they must be reconciled to one answer before both nodes\n   are live. The contract comment states this openly rather than asserting a\n   byte-identity that does not hold.\n3. The sync write path (ProtocolProjectionDatabaseSync) binds `timestamp` as an\n   ISO string. Real Postgres rejects that against a TIMESTAMPTZ column\n   (`invalid input for query argument`). It is PRE-EXISTING, out of this\n   ticket's scope, and unreachable in the runtime today because no shipped sync\n   adapter talks to a real database -- only InmemoryDatabaseAdapter does. The\n   real-Postgres test below normalizes exactly that one class of bind, and\n   deliberately does NOT normalize tenant_id, so the identity assertion is real.\n\nREAL-POSTGRES PROOF (projection-write-path-db-gate, satisfied not annotated)\nThe pre-commit gate refused the first version of this diff: \"touches a\nprojection write-path file but includes no accompanying real-Postgres\nintegration test change. A mock-DB-only test cannot catch a str-vs-datetime\ncolumn-type mismatch (OMN-15905).\" It was right -- every test in\ntest_omn16804_registry_resolved_write_tenant.py drives\nInmemoryDatabaseAdapter, a dict of lists that stores a `str` tenant as happily\nas a UUID, and delegation_events.tenant_id is `uuid` post-conversion.\n\ntests/test_omn16804_registry_resolved_write_tenant_real_postgres.py answers it:\na disposable schema, the FULL live migration set for this node (proven\nnecessary, not assumed -- the base three raise\n`UndefinedColumnError: column \"context_pack_hash\" does not exist`), the\npost-0032 tenant_id -> uuid conversion including the policy drop/recreate the\ncolumn type change requires, and the real HandlerProjectionDelegation driven\nthrough a thin sync asyncpg shim. It asserts the stored tenant_id is an actual\n`uuid.UUID` equal to the registry's, and that an unprovisioned tenant leaves NO\nrow behind -- the consequence in the table, not just the raise.\n\nExecuted against postgres:16, both tests: 2 passed.\n\n* chore(OMN-16804): bump the source-derived declared-table golden count for the tenant_registry_mirror read accessor\n\nRebase onto origin/dev; node_projection_delegation's new read-only\ndb_io declaration of tenant_registry_mirror (OMN-16804) is this\nbranch's first declaration of that relation (the owning write\ndeclaration lands separately on OMN-16930's branch, not yet merged\nhere), so classification_status is 'blocked' and only\nsource_declared_tables moves: 66 -> 67. Regenerated the checked-in\nOMN-15423 relation inventory to match.\n\n* test(OMN-16804): xfail(strict) the delegation-write chain-gate case pending the tenant_registry_mirror grant\n\nnode_projection_delegation's new OMN-16804 read declaration of\ntenant_registry_mirror needs a topology TABLE grant (SELECT for\ntenant_projection_writer on public.tenant_registry_mirror) that\nomnibase_infra's generate_application_database_table_grants.py can\nonly generate against a PINNED omnimarket release carrying this\ncontract (unreleased). Two of the three chain-gate tests were failing\noutright (ValueError from _require_projection_binding_privileges,\nraised before the already-documented tenant-authority-seam check the\nthird test's existing xfail covers). Applied the file's own sanctioned\nidiom -- xfail(strict=True) that flips XPASS the moment the grant\nlands -- per-case (only the delegation-write case touches this table;\nthe inference-response case must keep passing) via an imperative\nrequest.node.add_marker helper rather than a blanket decorator, since\npytest.mark.xfail on the shared parametrize would also mark the\nstill-passing case.\n\n* test(OMN-16804): configure fetchval on the delegation-runner mock DBs for the new registry lookup\n\nOMN-16804's write-tenant resolver now calls db.fetchval() against\ntenant_registry_mirror before falling back to the closed legacy map.\nBoth files' mock database fixtures left fetchval unconfigured, so an\nautospec/AsyncMock returned another mock instance instead of None,\nwhich _coerce_registry_uuid correctly refuses as not a UUID -- two\ntests using the legacy slug 'beta-business-proof' failed on that,\nnot on anything the tests themselves assert. Configured fetchval to\nreturn None (mirror has no row for this slug), which is the correct\nstand-in for these fixtures and lets resolution fall through to the\nlegacy map exactly as before OMN-16804.\n\n* test(OMN-16804): mark delegation seam grant pending explicitly\n\n* chore(OMN-16804): bump omnimarket after dependency release\n\n* test(OMN-16804): patch registry tenant resolver mutation\n\n* test(OMN-16804): guard redundant tenant uuid conversion\n\n* test(OMN-16804): satisfy CodeQL registry proof checks","verified_at":"2026-08-31T10:01:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/fd3e66c71ccfd4f7383904baa19e5bd700993a05","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/fd3e66c71ccfd4f7383904baa19e5bd700993a05","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/fd3e66c71ccfd4f7383904baa19e5bd700993a05/comments","author":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7f082ebd4742832d8f19f66182546a100c6e5ba0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/7f082ebd4742832d8f19f66182546a100c6e5ba0","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/7f082ebd4742832d8f19f66182546a100c6e5ba0"}]},"merge_base_commit":{"sha":"2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd","node_id":"C_kwDOR6jjtdoAKDJmMTIzYjRjMDFlYWJkMmM1MWY3ZDcwMzQ5MWU5Y2RmMzZmODliY2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jonah Gray","email":"jonah@omninode.ai","date":"2026-08-31T06:43:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-31T06:43:09Z"},"message":"feat(OMN-17019): obligation-kind work events + open-obligations projection (C9) (#2227)\n\n* feat(OMN-17019): obligation-kind work events + open-obligations projection\n\nC9 of the OMN-16176 ledger ladder. Replaces \"a markdown file is the goal and\nqueue authority\" with typed obligation events and a materialized projection.\n\nFive obligation kinds (created / transferred / satisfied / superseded /\nabandoned) registered in the emit registry under the EXISTING\nonex.evt.omniclaude.* producer namespace -- no bespoke topic family -- all\npartitioned on obligation_id and all duty_critical, because obligation writes\nfail closed.\n\nnode_projection_open_obligations folds them into\nomninode_internal.open_obligations, one row per obligation. Each kind writes\nonly the columns its kind owns; state and owed_by are GENERATED columns over\nthose facts. That is what makes a consumer restarting from an earlier\npartition offset unable to reopen a closed obligation -- the case a writable\nstate column would silently get wrong.\n\nobligations_view.py renders the B1/B2/A6/A14 surfaces as pure functions over\nthe projection, with render/parse exact inverses so \"delete it and regenerate\nit\" is mechanically testable.\n\nNo expiry, no TTL, no DELETE anywhere: an obligation leaves the open set only\nvia a recorded terminal event naming its own evidence.\n\n* test(OMN-17019): advance the two registry-growth ratchets deliberately\n\nThe full-suite escalation surfaced two ratchets that exist precisely to force\na deliberate decision when the emit registry grows, and the five new\nwork-obligation kinds tripped both. Both are advanced here with the decision\nrecorded, not auto-followed.\n\n1. _DUTY_CRITICAL_ALLOWLIST gains the five obligation kinds. duty_critical is\n   the load-bearing choice of this ticket -- an obligation READ may degrade to\n   the last-good projection and say so, but an obligation WRITE fails closed;\n   the telemetry tier permits exactly the silent drop C9 exists to end. The\n   ratchet's max_payload obligation is specific to the two CAPTURE topics,\n   which carry arbitrary artifact/tool output; every field of an obligation\n   event is a short scalar, bounded by its own schema.\n\n2. test_enrichment_parity's four counts move 62->67 event types and 65->70\n   published records / enriched records, with the null-key remainder frozen at\n   2 because all five obligation kinds declare partition_key_field:\n   obligation_id. Raising these WIDENS the byte-identical parity proof to\n   cover the new kinds rather than excusing them from it -- the mismatched\n   assertion still runs over all 67.\n\n* fix(OMN-17019): bind open obligations publish topic in handler\n\n* fix(OMN-17019): mark open-obligations applied event terminal\n\n* chore(OMN-17019): bump package version for release identity","tree":{"sha":"f2684e63e3cab4e4430af47dc315c5a134fefa99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/trees/f2684e63e3cab4e4430af47dc315c5a134fefa99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/commits/2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlSJ9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAss4QAA4VMn+iinUG5iBR3+LuikxA\nPVr+nQPyUgxryCg2wJMa5YY1mhaP+w5ASw1GOQwb7Jt9scr0oa7KK0CSIaXPOWdC\nVu+eVY6je7xwJorhMWAZMgOayEAO1TXayZvyTHodDwLMIFDGQIfwv+N7Iu2Mxtqi\nUuuCDN99vIKiHzNXCqRFJo5Y6s7K3dCx1PlBuYfbT5j2+O24cazCGx+Xk472/yxT\n+D7dNLPT5+gNhX1FexqI96yQU0QmExGV3rp2WwJt5FmLntrP3ZJD70VKXCjK/TMk\nQgL33tuUHCYNMthiKi7megQ5g6DG6Op1R/c6R7szhODuuOs/f5FpEE+uaG6KePeh\nDdCegwh9iclRDA4ZWmxQHj7mVBQjO6O2UGPyz/oUI5wPk0DIDZXspzajZabhr+FC\nckghbEGzRvSMBO6OFXdeztWWsHCihJJ3HZIgB9hppS5/2kiIptfdif901/F2NCcP\nS1Lk6TTHDyc3Tvf/Bm1PU5vz+Tv40zi7Ak5dGgpn0acQkCiKpj3hlHjjYy3fDm6V\nLdBo76S0o1v/a/XJx3zNW6A0FjdubXbfOPjzm1H+xFRYfNzunY7xwZA9l7jTHjV1\nsXGlbsjmEbbwMdsBuWNskFzbnSzIVZCN1SIEXWgArHfGVXh35zQiEOvyFWN2EKKD\nqck/LReMKaBKmAlQzMm7\n=JRh0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f2684e63e3cab4e4430af47dc315c5a134fefa99\nparent 4dcd92ee5f6a7d21339e0f3d599bc1fe94d357f1\nauthor Jonah Gray <jonah@omninode.ai> 1788158589 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788158589 +0000\n\nfeat(OMN-17019): obligation-kind work events + open-obligations projection (C9) (#2227)\n\n* feat(OMN-17019): obligation-kind work events + open-obligations projection\n\nC9 of the OMN-16176 ledger ladder. Replaces \"a markdown file is the goal and\nqueue authority\" with typed obligation events and a materialized projection.\n\nFive obligation kinds (created / transferred / satisfied / superseded /\nabandoned) registered in the emit registry under the EXISTING\nonex.evt.omniclaude.* producer namespace -- no bespoke topic family -- all\npartitioned on obligation_id and all duty_critical, because obligation writes\nfail closed.\n\nnode_projection_open_obligations folds them into\nomninode_internal.open_obligations, one row per obligation. Each kind writes\nonly the columns its kind owns; state and owed_by are GENERATED columns over\nthose facts. That is what makes a consumer restarting from an earlier\npartition offset unable to reopen a closed obligation -- the case a writable\nstate column would silently get wrong.\n\nobligations_view.py renders the B1/B2/A6/A14 surfaces as pure functions over\nthe projection, with render/parse exact inverses so \"delete it and regenerate\nit\" is mechanically testable.\n\nNo expiry, no TTL, no DELETE anywhere: an obligation leaves the open set only\nvia a recorded terminal event naming its own evidence.\n\n* test(OMN-17019): advance the two registry-growth ratchets deliberately\n\nThe full-suite escalation surfaced two ratchets that exist precisely to force\na deliberate decision when the emit registry grows, and the five new\nwork-obligation kinds tripped both. Both are advanced here with the decision\nrecorded, not auto-followed.\n\n1. _DUTY_CRITICAL_ALLOWLIST gains the five obligation kinds. duty_critical is\n   the load-bearing choice of this ticket -- an obligation READ may degrade to\n   the last-good projection and say so, but an obligation WRITE fails closed;\n   the telemetry tier permits exactly the silent drop C9 exists to end. The\n   ratchet's max_payload obligation is specific to the two CAPTURE topics,\n   which carry arbitrary artifact/tool output; every field of an obligation\n   event is a short scalar, bounded by its own schema.\n\n2. test_enrichment_parity's four counts move 62->67 event types and 65->70\n   published records / enriched records, with the null-key remainder frozen at\n   2 because all five obligation kinds declare partition_key_field:\n   obligation_id. Raising these WIDENS the byte-identical parity proof to\n   cover the new kinds rather than excusing them from it -- the mismatched\n   assertion still runs over all 67.\n\n* fix(OMN-17019): bind open obligations publish topic in handler\n\n* fix(OMN-17019): mark open-obligations applied event terminal\n\n* chore(OMN-17019): bump package version for release identity","verified_at":"2026-08-31T06:43:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/2f123b4c01eabd2c51f7d703491e9cdf36f89bcd/comments","author":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4dcd92ee5f6a7d21339e0f3d599bc1fe94d357f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit